"whatsNew.title" = "What's New";
"whatsNew.v100.baseline.detail" = "Today is measured against your best day in thirty, this month against the same days last month, all time against the next milestone. Every card says what it is comparing against. A full ring means you beat your own record — never a warning, and there is nothing here to run out of.";
"whatsNew.v100.baseline.title" = "The arcs mean something";
"whatsNew.v100.headline" = "What every plan has paid back, at a glance";
"whatsNew.v100.local.detail" = "tokscale ships inside the app (MIT) — no Homebrew, no npm, no node. Entirely local: it never opens the keychain, never asks for a password, and nothing leaves this Mac.";
"whatsNew.v100.local.title" = "Nothing to install, nothing sent anywhere";
"whatsNew.v100.makers.detail" = "The same model reached through different routes collapses into one row, a locally-run Qwen still counts as Qwen, and a plan-billed GLM is no longer credited to somebody else.";
"whatsNew.v100.makers.title" = "Counted by who made the model";
"whatsNew.v100.payback.detail" = "Tell TokNotch what a plan costs and when it renews, and its card shows how many times over your usage has repaid it — 13.4× paid back, or $18 to go. Priced at what the same work would have cost on the published API rates, and counted by the real billing period rather than the calendar month.";
"whatsNew.v100.payback.title" = "Did the plan pay for itself?";
"whatsNew.v100.rings.detail" = "Three rings that stay at the edge of the screen. Under each is the token count; reach for one and the card shows equivalent value, the input and output split, how many requests, and the models used most.";
"whatsNew.v100.rings.title" = "Today · This month · All time";
"whatsNew.v100.vendors.detail" = "Anthropic, OpenAI, DeepSeek, Qwen and the rest — one ring each, all off until you ask for them. The list is built from what this Mac has actually run, so a company you have never used never appears.";
"whatsNew.v100.vendors.title" = "A ring per vendor, only where it's earned";
"whatsNew.v110.headline" = "Keeps itself up to date, and speaks your language";
"whatsNew.v110.icon.detail" = "The app icon now comes with a dark or a light frame. Choose the one you like in Settings.";
"whatsNew.v110.icon.title" = "Pick your icon";
"whatsNew.v110.languages.detail" = "Arabic, Italian, Dutch, Polish, Brazilian Portuguese, Turkish and Vietnamese join the nine already here, each writing numbers, money and dates its own way.";
"whatsNew.v110.languages.title" = "Sixteen languages";
"whatsNew.v110.simpler.detail" = "TokNotch now opens with your Mac on its own, and settings only speak up when something needs you.";
"whatsNew.v110.simpler.title" = "Fewer things to set";
"whatsNew.v110.updates.detail" = "TokNotch now checks for new versions by itself and installs them in place, signed and notarized by Apple, so the numbers keep matching the tools you use.";
"whatsNew.v110.updates.title" = "Updates arrive on their own";
"whatsNew.v120.headline" = "Your payback at a glance, with less to set";
"whatsNew.v120.menuBar.detail" = "TokNotch no longer takes a spot in the Dock. Its menu bar icon shows this period's payback and today's tokens at a glance.";
"whatsNew.v120.menuBar.title" = "Lives in the menu bar";
"whatsNew.v120.payback.detail" = "Every vendor sits on one line with its plan, renewal day, payback multiple and ring switch. Details like a custom price appear only when you need them.";
"whatsNew.v120.payback.title" = "Payback on one page";
"whatsNew.v120.simpler.detail" = "Settings is now one page for the notch, language and icon. The hidden mode is gone, so the notch is always within reach.";
"whatsNew.v120.simpler.title" = "Fewer choices to make";
"whatsNew.v121.about.detail" = "Open it from the menu bar or the version in Settings to see the icon at full size.";
"whatsNew.v121.about.title" = "An About window";
"whatsNew.v121.colours.detail" = "A plan's payback multiple is now drawn in that vendor's colour, so Claude and OpenAI never look alike.";
"whatsNew.v121.colours.title" = "Each vendor in its own colour";
"whatsNew.v121.fold.title" = "The settings arc folds away with the notch";
"whatsNew.v121.headline" = "Small things, done properly";
"whatsNew.v122.headline" = "Meet the other apps";
"whatsNew.v122.more.detail" = "The foot of Settings now shows the other apps Reff Wu makes, each one ready to get or open.";
"whatsNew.v122.more.title" = "More from Reff Wu";
"whatsNew.v123.antigravity.detail" = "TokNotch now syncs Antigravity every few minutes, so its Gemini usage no longer stops updating.";
"whatsNew.v123.antigravity.title" = "Antigravity usage keeps up";
"whatsNew.v123.headline" = "Every tool, kept current";
"whatsNew.v123.tokscale.title" = "Built on tokscale 4.16";
"whatsNew.v124.headline" = "Updates take care of themselves";
